SELECT 
  d_week_seq, 
  ss_store_sk, 
  SUM(ss_sales_price) FILTER (WHERE d_day_name = 'Sunday') AS sun_sales,
  SUM(ss_sales_price) FILTER (WHERE d_day_name = 'Monday') AS mon_sales,
  ...
FROM 
  store_sales
GROUP BY 
  d_week_seq, 
  ss_store_sk;
```

In the rewritten query, we replaced each CASE expression with a single aggregate function using a FILTER clause. This simplifies the query and makes it more efficient to execute.
